### Health check
GET http://127.0.0.1:8000/

### Register a sensor
POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/devices
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "serial": "SH-000123",
  "name": "Serra 3 - sonda nord",
  "device_class": "sensor",
  "site": "Sezze"
}

> {% client.global.set("device_id", response.body.data.id); %}

### Count and list (the data survive a server restart)
GET http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/devices/count?site=Sezze

###
GET http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/devices/list?site=Sezze&offset=0&limit=10

### Read the desired configuration (note the version)
GET http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/devices/{{device_id}}/config

### Save a new configuration with the version just read -> 200, version + 1
PUT http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/devices/{{device_id}}/config
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "version": 1,
  "min_temp": 12,
  "max_temp": 28,
  "sampling_sec": 30
}

### Same request again (stale version) -> 409 Conflict
PUT http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/devices/{{device_id}}/config
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "version": 1,
  "min_temp": 14,
  "max_temp": 26,
  "sampling_sec": 30
}

### min_temp >= max_temp -> 422
PUT http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/devices/{{device_id}}/config
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "version": 2,
  "min_temp": 30,
  "max_temp": 20,
  "sampling_sec": 30
}
